                report.opened_translated = false;
                report.errors.push("in-place overwrite ABORTED (fail-closed): could not verify pre-overwrite backup — " + __backupGate.error);
                plog("AC9 backup gate FAILED → abort overwrite: " + __backupGate.error);
                // 🔴 Say what the operator can SEE, not just what we intended.
                // The old wording ("your document on disk was NOT modified.
                // In-memory changes remain") is literally true and still reads
                // as "nothing happened" — while the document in front of the
                // operator is fully translated. 2026-08-28 the owner reported
                // this alert as "it said aborted but it wrote anyway": nothing
                // wrote the disk, but the open doc looked like a success, and
                // one Ctrl+S would have COMPLETED the overwrite this gate
                // refused — with no backup, which is the exact loss AC9 exists
                // to prevent. An abort notice the operator can defeat by
                // pressing Save has to say so.
                //
                // 🔴 2026-08-28, second pass: the first version of THIS rewrite still said
                // "Press Ctrl+Z once to discard" — inherited from the old text, and made
                // WORSE by the word "once". The source says otherwise: this file opens up
                // to THREE separate ENTIRE_SCRIPT blocks (2130 "Import v2 Pipeline" · 2666
                // "byPair re-sweep" · 3026 missing-font remap), and ProjectMetaLabel.write
                // / ProjectUid.ensureUid mutate the doc AFTER all of them. The owner run
